| Workspace QA | `tests/` (Playwright — `contract` + `marketplace` projects) |
| Design records | `Docs/DESIGN_RECORDS/` |

Product repos **consume** governance; they must not fork conflicting Dewey, versioning, or reusable pipeline rules.

## Standing invariants

- Every SubTerraCo repo uses **`master`** as its default branch (constitution §4.1). Do not invent another production-branch name.
- New application code is **TypeScript**. Python is allowed only when the work needs Python. Config and tooling files that the tool itself requires to be JavaScript may stay JavaScript (constitution §14).
- All SubTerra repos live under **`SubTerraCo`** (Team plan required for private-repo reusable workflows).
- Twin SDKs (`@subterra/app-sdk`, `@subterra/integration-sdk`) must export identical symbol names equal to `SDK_SURFACE`, differing only in `SDK_ROLE`. Change the surface in `sdk-contract` and mirror into both twins.
- Vendor upstreams are a separate `upstream` remote — `origin` is always our own repo.
- Manifest **`audience`** (`admin` / `member`) gates which shell may mount an item; default `["admin"]` fail-closed. Never overload SDK `role` for permissions (GV-0002).
- NFC login must be **challenge-response** (ECDSA); UID-only auth is forbidden (constitution §13).
- SubTerra-owned UI uses **Material Design 3** tokens from `packages/ui` (seed `#e8a54b`). Tailwind carries those tokens. Do not add a second component library (constitution §15, GV-0004).
- The enterprise monorepo uses `main`. Existing repos stay on `master`. New original monorepo code is BSL 1.1. MIT upstream and already published MIT grants stay MIT (constitution §16).

## When working here

- Prefer changes in `governance/` that product repos can adopt via template / workflow ref / `@subterra/ci-ops`.
- Register every new app/integration in APP_REGISTRY + manifest before scaffolding GitHub.
- Keep product-local e2e in the product repo; keep **cross-repo contract** e2e in governance.
- Follow CI_OPS Round 1/2 design gates for `/NF` `/NB` `/RD` and multi-option locks (AskQuestion when available).

## Out of scope unless explicitly asked

Implementing feature UI inside Blocks, Shell product screens, Mailbot logic, or Anytype integration handlers — route those to the owning APP code agent.